      "location": "frontmatter physical_scope, bounded-domain uniqueness claim",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The physical_scope asserts that 'a Coulomb-gauge representative with prescribed smooth parameter-dependent Dirichlet data exists uniquely on the physical region'. Statement (b) permits an 'arbitrary interval' I and requires ψ=g_D only on ∂Ω×I. Take Ω to be the unit ball, I={0}, the original ambient potential pair (0,0), and g_D=0. The smooth ambient generators ψ₁(x,t)=0 and ψ₂(x,t)=t both satisfy Δψ=0 and the prescribed boundary values at the physical time. Their restrictions as generator functions coincide, but their ambient gauge transforms restrict to distinct Coulomb representatives (0,0) and (-1,0), both with zero fields. Thus uniqueness of generator values on Ω×I, which the proof establishes, does not imply the asserted uniqueness of the potential representative when I is a singleton.",
